{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "docs_hub_schedule_hub_schedule",
      "label": "The hub schedule",
      "file_type": "document",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\hub-schedule.md",
      "source_location": "L1-5",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "In REBUILT your alliance HUB stops scoring for part of teleop. The console works out when from the rules and the FMS game data, so the robot does not have to tell it."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_hub_schedule_six_segments",
      "label": "Six teleop segments, Table 6-2",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\hub-schedule.md",
      "source_location": "L12-22",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Teleop runs 140 s in six segments. The clock counts down, so each segment is named by the time remaining when it ends: transition 2:20-2:10, shifts 1-4 at 25 s each, end game 0:30-0:00."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_hub_schedule_alternating_shifts",
      "label": "Alternating shifts 1-4",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\hub-schedule.md",
      "source_location": "L24-25",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "The alliance that scored more fuel in AUTO is inactive for shift 1, then they alternate. On a tie FMS picks one at random, so the game data always names an alliance."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_hub_schedule_game_data_arrives_late",
      "label": "Game data is empty until after auto",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\hub-schedule.md",
      "source_location": "L29-35",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "/FMSInfo/GameSpecificMessage is a single character, R or B, naming the alliance whose goal goes inactive first. It is empty until roughly three seconds after auto ends, once fuel scoring has been assessed. That is why the tile says waiting for FMS game data early in a match rather than guessing."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_hub_schedule_no_game_data_needed",
      "label": "Auto, transition and end game need no game data",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\hub-schedule.md",
      "source_location": "L34-35",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Both hubs are active by rule in those segments, and the tile says so rather than reporting an unknown. The schedule is only genuinely underdetermined during shifts 1-4."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_hub_schedule_fmsinfo_carries_no_clock",
      "label": "/FMSInfo carries no match clock",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\hub-schedule.md",
      "source_location": "L38-46",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "That table has the control word, the alliance, the event and the game-specific message but no time. Robot code has to publish it with CatalystLog.log(\"Match/TimeLeft\", DriverStation.getMatchTime()). Without it the timer and the hub countdown show dashes rather than inventing a number."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_installing_installing",
      "label": "Installing Catalyst Console",
      "file_type": "document",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\installing.md",
      "source_location": "L1-3",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Three ways in, in the order most teams should pick: with the Catalyst desktop app, the standalone installer, or from source."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_installing_bundled_with_catalyst_app",
      "label": "Bundled with the Catalyst desktop app",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\installing.md",
      "source_location": "L5-16",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "A Driver Console entry appears in the sidebar. The console is a separate binary with its own release cadence, so the app asks whether one is bundled rather than offering a button that reports not found when pressed."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_installing_standalone_installer",
      "label": "The standalone installer",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\installing.md",
      "source_location": "L18-25",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "About 3.5 MB, Start Menu entry and desktop shortcut. The usual case for the machine that actually runs matches."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_installing_from_source",
      "label": "Building from source",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\installing.md",
      "source_location": "L26-40",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "npm install, npm run vendor, npm run build. Needs Rust and the WebView2 runtime that ships with Windows 11."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_installing_optional_field_bakes",
      "label": "The optional field bakes",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\installing.md",
      "source_location": "L42-50",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "npm run field-cad bakes the KOP field CAD down to something a dashboard can carry; npm run field-collision derives collision geometry from it. Both optional — without them the field view draws itself from published dimensions."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_installing_quiet_update_check",
      "label": "The quiet update check",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\installing.md",
      "source_location": "L72-80",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "The console looks once at launch, quietly. If there is one a chip appears in the dock; if the machine cannot reach GitHub — on a field network the normal case — nothing appears at all. No prompt, no dialog, no interruption anywhere in this path, because an update notice is exactly the sort of thing rule two exists to keep away from a driver."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_installing_signed_releases",
      "label": "Signed releases",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\installing.md",
      "source_location": "L82-83",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Releases are signed and the installer verifies the signature, so an update tampered with in transit is refused rather than run."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_mcp_diagnostics_server",
      "label": "The diagnostics MCP server",
      "file_type": "document",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\mcp.md",
      "source_location": "L1-11",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Started with --mcp it opens no window: it connects to NetworkTables exactly as the dashboard does and speaks the Model Context Protocol on stdin and stdout, so an agent can ask what the robot is publishing."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_mcp_no_drive_tool",
      "label": "There is no drive tool, and there will not be one",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\mcp.md",
      "source_location": "L13-30",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Every tool reads, none writes. No enable, no drive, no estop, and no nt_set either. The dashboard's own NetworkTables write path exists for tunables and auto choosers, is guarded against /FMSInfo, and is deliberately not reachable from mcp.rs. That is the first of the three rules holding, not a feature nobody got round to."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_mcp_diagnosis_needs_no_control",
      "label": "Diagnosis has never needed control",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\mcp.md",
      "source_location": "L28-30",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "What the server is for is the other half of the problem: an agent that can see the robot's state can diagnose it. The argument that lets rule 1 and a useful agent surface coexist."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_mcp_tool_surface",
      "label": "The nine read-only tools",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\mcp.md",
      "source_location": "L66-81",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "console_status, nt_list, nt_get, alerts, physics, match_state, ds_sessions, ds_events, field_map. Start with console_status: every other tool reads more usefully once you know whether there is a robot on the other end."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_mcp_absent_is_not_zero",
      "label": "Absent is not zero",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\mcp.md",
      "source_location": "L83-93",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "The third rule applies here more than anywhere, because an agent cannot see the dash a driver would. A tile that shows an em dash is obviously empty; a tool that returns 0.0 is confidently wrong, and an agent will act on it. So every value carries whether it was actually published."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_mcp_alerts_null_not_empty_list",
      "label": "alerts returns null, not an empty list",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\mcp.md",
      "source_location": "L97-99",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "An empty list reads as all clear, which is the most dangerous wrong answer this server could give. A missing group means the question was not answered, not that the robot is healthy."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_mcp_mode_null_without_control_word",
      "label": "match_state.mode is null without a control word",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\mcp.md",
      "source_location": "L100-101",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Not \"Disabled\". A robot nobody is hearing from is not a robot that is disabled."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_mcp_empty_game_message_is_published",
      "label": "Published-and-empty is not absent",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\mcp.md",
      "source_location": "L102-103",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "FMS sends the game-specific message at the start of teleop, and the hub schedule depends on telling an empty published string apart from an absent topic."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_mcp_rtt_null_while_disconnected",
      "label": "console_status.rtt_ms is null while disconnected",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\mcp.md",
      "source_location": "L104-105",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "A round trip measured on a link that has since dropped is a stale number, not a current one."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_mcp_nan_as_string",
      "label": "NaN comes back as the string \"NaN\"",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\mcp.md",
      "source_location": "L106-109",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "JSON has no NaN and serialisers turn it into null — which in this server means not published. An uninitialised estimator publishes NaN often enough that conflating the two would be a real misreading. The type is still reported as double."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_mcp_quiet_session_versus_unreadable",
      "label": "A quiet session is not an unreadable file",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\mcp.md",
      "source_location": "L110-112",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "The .dslog formats are community-reverse-engineered rather than documented by NI, so a header the parser does not recognise is reported as unparsed rather than decoded into plausible nonsense."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_mcp_field_map_says_where_it_looked",
      "label": "field_map says which paths it searched",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\mcp.md",
      "source_location": "L113-115",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "The map is generated by npm run field-collision and is deliberately not committed, so a fresh checkout and an installed build both legitimately lack one. Saying where it looked turns an absence into an answer."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_mcp_advisory_travels_with_numbers",
      "label": "The advisory travels with the numbers",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\mcp.md",
      "source_location": "L136-138",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "The Physics Core tile says advisory only on its face for a driver; an agent reading the same values deserves the same warning, and unlike a driver it cannot see the tile."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_mcp_no_sdk_dependency",
      "label": "Implemented without an MCP SDK",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\mcp.md",
      "source_location": "L145-147",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "The surface a server this small needs is a few hundred lines, and a dependency for it would be more code to audit than the code it replaces, in a binary that ships to a driver station laptop."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_mcp_stdout_is_protocol_only",
      "label": "stdout carries protocol frames and nothing else",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\mcp.md",
      "source_location": "L149-150",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Anything else on stdout corrupts the stream. Diagnostics for humans, and the NetworkTables client's own logging, go to stderr."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_mcp_jsonrpc_over_stdio",
      "label": "JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\mcp.md",
      "source_location": "L140-143",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "One JSON object per line: initialize, tools/list, tools/call and ping. Protocol revisions 2024-11-05, 2025-03-26 and 2025-06-18 are all answered."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_mcp_two_nt_clients_are_fine",
      "label": "Two NetworkTables clients are ordinary",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\mcp.md",
      "source_location": "L62-64",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Running the server alongside the dashboard is fine — Shuffleboard and Glass coexist the same way. What must not be duplicated is the Driver Station, and neither of them is one. The distinction that makes rule 1 about control rather than about connections."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_mcp_failure_is_quiet_and_honest",
      "label": "Failure, quietly and without lying",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\yu_th\\dev\\CatalystConsole\\docs\\mcp.md",
      "source_location": "L161-168",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "No robot is the normal state for most of a day and is not an error — the tools answer with connected:false and report the absence of each value rather than failing the call. The NetworkTables client reconnects on its own forever."
    }
  ],
